-- Whether the allowance is paid depends on `resident`, but how much depends
-- on `income`, which no condition reads. No condition mentions a number, so
-- the report tries `income` at zero alone, and says which input that is
-- rather than let one printed answer stand for every income.
GIVEN income IS A NUMBER
      resident IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `allowance` IS
  IF resident THEN income TIMES 0.1 ELSE 0
